WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.240
Speaker 1: A former gas station manager in&nbsp;
California is out of a job right now after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:11.440
making the mistake of selling premium gasoline for&nbsp;
$0.69 a gallon instead of $6.99 a gallon. The man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:15.920
in question is name's John Suzanna, and he worked&nbsp;
at a Shell station in Rancho Cordova, California.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:20.720
Once customers realized that there was a&nbsp;
mistake, they flooded to the gas station. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:25.280
what didn't, you know, they were totally willing&nbsp;
to take advantage of that 90% discounted gasoline.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:29.760
I'm surprised they didn't show up with buckets and&nbsp;
everything else. They could store that gas because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:34.000
prices for gasoline right now are at record&nbsp;
highs, especially over in California, $7 plus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.200
per gallon. You'd think that they would try to do&nbsp;
all they could. But the problem is obviously that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:44.240
nothing comes for free. And this was a small,&nbsp;
independently owned gas station and ultimately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:49.760
there were about $20,000 in losses that resulted&nbsp;
from all of this. Susanna said about this, quote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:54.880
Once I realized what was going on, I immediately&nbsp;
thought we had been robbed. And I was scared that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:59.520
something terrible had happened to the cashiers.&nbsp;
He was unfortunately fired over this mistake,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:04.000
and he said about it, quote, Even though it cost&nbsp;
me my job, it's fine. Because the truth is, you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:08.400
know, it was my fault. So he's definitely in good&nbsp;
spirits over this. And you can't help but feel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:13.600
bad for this guy. Everyone makes mistakes, right?&nbsp;
Everyone types in the wrong number here and there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:18.800
Everyone will put in a typo. And for this guy,&nbsp;
it just happened to result in $20,000 in losses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:23.600
for his company. Now, for most people, that's&nbsp;
where the story would end. But in John's case, it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.120
actually continued because his sister felt so bad&nbsp;
about it that she decided to set up a go fund me&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:36.640
to help the newly unemployed John make up the&nbsp;
lost funds to his former employer. The Go Fund&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:41.440
Me was hugely successful. It surpassed the&nbsp;
$20,000 mark that they were trying to raise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:47.040
actually reaching and surpassing $24,000. John&nbsp;
sister said about this, quote, He doesn't have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:50.720
to pay it back. But just the fact that he is&nbsp;
doing it and wants to do it shows a lot of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:55.280
character and honesty and responsibility. And I'm&nbsp;
really proud of him for that. You got to wonder,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:59.040
how can this guy stay fired, right? Like,&nbsp;
for one, this was an honest mistake, which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:03.680
I understand. Sometimes people can get fired for&nbsp;
honest mistakes. Honest mistakes can kill people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:09.920
or they can, as in this case, cost a company&nbsp;
$20,000. But then even after all of that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:14.160
he didn't become a disgruntled former employee&nbsp;
like most people would do in that circumstance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:18.400
No, he raised the money not to pay for&nbsp;
his own living expenses, but to pay back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:22.480
his former employer and then some. Right.&nbsp;
Because he actually raised $24,000.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:28.400
So if anyone deserves their job back, it's this&nbsp;
guy. Maybe if he's not able to get the job back at&nbsp;&nbsp;

